	<td bgcolor="#111111" width="100%" valign="top">
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" > <b></b></font>
	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" ><blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr><br />
I do care about VE, I've been up front and clear about that from post one. I don't care what mobs Hoss has killed or planes Hoss has visited, I've been clear on that too. You seem to have confused the two.<br />
<br />
As to why defend myself or VE - I do so because lies unconfronted are sometimes believed. I do so because I'm proud of VE and the decency that it stands for.<br />
<hr></blockquote><br />
<br />
Stands for decency?  What are you, the Justice League?  This is a GAME, dammit.  You are attaching significance to something that means absolutely nil here.  There are "good people" and "bad people" in every environment you can imagine.  How on earth does "standing for decency" in a video game accomplish anything?  Does it imply that you are NOT a decent person outside the confines of that game?<br />
<br />
You've had your feelings hurt that someone thinks that you're a political jackass.  Whooptee fuckin' doo.  Yet you feel the need to come onto MY boards and post these epic length diatribes about how you will defend your guild's reputation and stand for decency.  Stand against whom?  Who exactly are these "indecent" folk that you are taking such a heroic stand against?  Why does your opinion mean anything to me, or anyone else who reads this board?  Why are you here?<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr><br />
What you see as stirring up shit others see as a valid critique of Andaas' proposal. That you in particular jumped up and started threatening people over a topic with a clear conflict of interest is something no good moderator does, precisely because it opens them up to criticisms of bias. Either you don't realize that, which makes you a poor moderator, or you do realize it and don't care, which is worse.<br />
<hr></blockquote><br />
<br />
When did you get this cockeyed idea that I'm a moderator?  Do you know what an administrator is?  Do you know what a moderator is?  Don't mistake the fact that I can perform "moderator" functions with my role as an admin here.  I ain't your referee, and I ain't your babysitter. My job is to see that this board remains entertaining for the people who participate here.  I have never attempted to please everyone or be "fair".  The people that I get rid of are people who contribute nothing to the boards and whose presense here causes other participants to leave.  Why on earth would I ban your dumb ass for expressing an opinion, misguided as it is?  You entertain me.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr><br />
For one to succeed on one's merits there must be rules that are fairly and equally enforced. Having the deck stacked, in the form of clearly and voiciferously biased moderators, does not allow one to fail on one's own merits, it makes one fail or succeed on the capricious whims of those who run the board. So far I have nothing to complain about about my success or failure, in that you have not used those powers in an unfair fashion, and am comfortable with the thread and where it has gone.<br />
<hr></blockquote><br />
<br />
Thank you for your opinion, but here in the real world, or at least the part of it known as the Internet, there are no rules.  You are a guest in my "home" and you play by my rules, whatever they may be. (hell, I don't know them all myself...)<br />
<br />
You don't walk into a bar, start a discussion, then insist that the other participants play by rules which you think are "fair".  You don't do that on these forums either.<br />
<br />
When in Rome, do as the Romans do.<br />
<br />
When on these forums, do as the Dorfs do.<br />
<br />
If coarse language and personal attacks in the face of a ludicrous argument bother you, then go play on the Yahoo boards or something.  As message boards go, this one runs a hell of a lot cleaner than most.  There's a reason for that, and I'm part of it.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr><br />
You may not care if someone posts lies or truthful statements about Hoss, and you may simply ignore such posts, or laugh them off, or say "hey, it's just a game". A significant portion of EQ players, including some really decent people, put being uber and seeing the zones you are seeing as their top priority, making such a strategy perfectly rational.<br />
<br />
I don't care whether or not Hosslings are here defending Hoss, praising Hoss, etc. It is none of my business. VE is my business, and as such I do respond. I want a to be in a guild that is proud of its public reputation, and be in a guild where public lies about the guild are just as publicly disproven, and truthful statements about any misbehavior by guildmates are accepted and dealt with. Which is why I adopt quite a different strategy than what you say Hoss does when it comes to dealing with things said about my guild in public.<br />
<hr></blockquote><br />
<br />
I've asked 3 times.<br />
<br />
Why do you care?<br />
<br />
I understand that you're HERE to defend your precious reputation.. But why does your reputation matter to you?<br />
<br />
It's a fair question.<br />
<br />
If Hosslings responded directly to every negative thing written about us, we wouldn't have time to play the game.  So why bother?<br />
<br />
In any social environment, etiquette and protocols are established to ease the interaction between people.  Since we don't deal with you in the game, why should we care what you think of us? <br />
<br />
I'll use Ragefire Alliance as an example, again...<br />
<br />
There were some who felt that I (and other Hoss clerics) should not be allowed to participate independently without the full support and participation of our guild.  Why?  Our coming to RA was an attempt to "play nice" with the rest of the server when EVERYBODY knew damn well we could take Ragefire anytime we wanted to.  Yet in return for our attempts at cooperation, we were met with skepticism, cynicism, and outright derision by many people including some of your guildies.  This is the kind of petty bullshit that I've been alluding to.<br />
<br />
Do you have any idea how many times we had to convince the rest of the guild NOT to take Ragefire from you guys?  <br />
<br />
Yet people like you insist on bringing up incidents in the past that mean nothing today. (or will the rest of the server stop sending "You killed teh sleeper" tells to us anytime soon?)<br />
<br />
Typically, such "boorish" (I like your word, therefore I'll steal it) behavior comes from folks who pride themseves on "decency" and "reputation".  The "crusaders" are usually those who squawk the loudest while saying the least.<br />
<br />
So you can see why your argument raises my hackles just a bit.  I've seen people like you before, and they've usually been nothing but a pain in the ass.  The real "nice guys" on this server don't NEED to come here and post in defense of some honor that doesn't exist.<br />
<br />
If I were to call Alihja a "KS'ing, con artist", you could be assured that I'd be shouted down so fast that another admin would delete the thread out of pity, only after I had been properly crucified.  A person's opinion doesn't need to be examined like witness' testimony.  People's bullshit detectors work just fine in most cases.  Spin artists like you only make the problem worse.<br />
<br />
The fact that you and Cardinal (and now.. me) have engaged in our little pissing match seems to have resulted in widespread apathy from the rest of the server.<br />
<br />
So much for your reputation, right?  Nobody cares.  Nobody's mind was changed.<br />
<br />
So I ask again.<br />
<br />
Why do YOU?<br />
<br />
-Grim</font></p>
	
