	<td bgcolor="#222222" width="175" valign="top" nowrap>
	<a name="post75245"></a>
	
	<font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" ><b>Juergen</b></font><br>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >Skeleton</font><br>
	<p>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >Registered: Oct 2002<br>
	Location: <br>
	Posts: 25</font></td>
	
	<td bgcolor="#222222" width="100%" valign="top">
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" > <b></b></font>
	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" ><blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr><i>Originally posted by Grimthorn </i><br />
[B]Stands for decency?  What are you, the Justice League?  This is a GAME, dammit.  You are attaching significance to something that means absolutely nil here.  There are "good people" and "bad people" in every environment you can imagine.  How on earth does "standing for decency" in a video game accomplish anything?<hr></blockquote>Well, one thing doing the decent thing accomplishes is that it generally keeps VE from being a topic of this forum most of the time. Since my presence raises your hackles, and your posts are of a style that I don't particularly enjoy, I think that is a good outcome for both of us.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>Does it imply that you are NOT a decent person outside the confines of that game?<hr></blockquote>Bringing IRL stuff into these boards is typically discouraged by you from what I understand. However, if you really want to talk about IRL stuff I'm willing to do that too.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>You've had your feelings hurt that someone thinks that you're a political jackass.  Whooptee fuckin' doo.  Yet you feel the need to come onto MY boards and post these epic length diatribes about how you will defend your guild's reputation and stand for decency.  Stand against whom?  Who exactly are these "indecent" folk that you are taking such a heroic stand against?  Why does your opinion mean anything to me, or anyone else who reads this board?  Why are you here?<hr></blockquote>Been over this already. I don't care if my opinion is meaningless to you. I care if lies are posted about me or my guild.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>My job is to see that this board remains entertaining for the people who participate here.  I have never attempted to please everyone or be "fair".  The people that I get rid of are people who contribute nothing to the boards and whose presense here causes other participants to leave.  Why on earth would I ban your dumb ass for expressing an opinion, misguided as it is?  You entertain me.<hr></blockquote>Well then we are both happy. I am happy to have disputed the falsehoods you and Cardinal posted, and you are entertained.  <br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>Thank you for your opinion, but here in the real world, or at least the part of it known as the Internet, there are no rules.  You are a guest in my "home" and you play by my rules, whatever they may be. (hell, I don't know them all myself...)<hr></blockquote>Yes, and in general I try to stay out of your home, precisely for the reasons given.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>I understand that you're HERE to defend your precious reputation.. But why does your reputation matter to you?<br />
<br />
It's a fair question.<br />
<br />
If Hosslings responded directly to every negative thing written about us, we wouldn't have time to play the game.  So why bother?<hr></blockquote>This is one of those questions that is pretty hard to answer for someone who doesn't have the same mindset. I guess the best answer I can come up with is that I feel it is important to do the right thing, even in game. I don't think KSing is right, or plooting, for example, so I don't do them, because such activities make the game less fun for me. If someone says I did them (or, by extension, the guild I belong to) then that too detracts from my enjoyment.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>In any social environment, etiquette and protocols are established to ease the interaction between people.  Since we don't deal with you in the game, why should we care what you think of us? <hr></blockquote>Already been over this. That you don't care what people post or say about Hoss is irrelevant to me. I care about what people post or say about VE. I've never argued that you should care in the slightest what people think of you - it is your choice.<br />
<br />
Judging by the number of posts on this forum by many people in defense of their guild in various threads, it is clear that many people do care about the reputation of their guild. So it seems a rather odd question for you to suddenly be asking now, unless you can't come up with anything better to attack me on.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>There were some who felt that I (and other Hoss clerics) should not be allowed to participate independently without the full support and participation of our guild.  Why?  Our coming to RA was an attempt to "play nice" with the rest of the server when EVERYBODY knew damn well we could take Ragefire anytime we wanted to.  Yet in return for our attempts at cooperation, we were met with skepticism, cynicism, and outright derision by many people including some of your guildies.  This is the kind of petty bullshit that I've been alluding to.<br />
<br />
Do you have any idea how many times we had to convince the rest of the guild NOT to take Ragefire from you guys?<hr></blockquote>The RA was well run and the people who administrated it made sure fair treatment was accorded to you and to the rest of the participants. The only times you got any flack was when you would demand special treatment.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>So you can see why your argument raises my hackles just a bit.  I've seen people like you before, and they've usually been nothing but a pain in the ass.  The real "nice guys" on this server don't NEED to come here and post in defense of some honor that doesn't exist.<hr></blockquote>I have no desire to participate here any more than necessary, which is why my post count is what it is (and half of it due to this thread). I don't come here and post about 99% of the time. The only time I really do post is when somebody posts falsehoods about VE.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>If I were to call Alihja a "KS'ing, con artist", you could be assured that I'd be shouted down so fast that another admin would delete the thread out of pity, only after I had been properly crucified.  A person's opinion doesn't need to be examined like witness' testimony.  People's bullshit detectors work just fine in most cases.  Spin artists like you only make the problem worse.<hr></blockquote>What spin have I put? I've disputed the following falsehoods or implications made by you or others:<ul><li>That VE has a Lodizal kill squad or spends any time going after Lodizal (false - a couple months ago one VE member helped a couple people from another guild kill Lodizal - and they engaged first and got the exp)<li>That VE has wasted a bunch of Behemoths or had 5x CRs vs Behemoths (false - we have attempted him twice, once immediately before a patch. And for our two attempts we had 2 CRs and some good learning to show for it)<li>That VE has held pickup/open flag raids and excluded Hoss members from them (false, VE flag raids are VE-only affairs. The only OOG we have flagged to my knowledge is a member's IRL wife.)</ul>The above is what I came here to do. The rest has just been you insulting me for doing so and me responding.<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>So much for your reputation, right?  Nobody cares.  Nobody's mind was changed.<br />
<br />
So I ask again.<br />
<br />
Why do YOU?<hr></blockquote>Since you ask again, I'll answer again, but I'll try another approach: You post a lot about what Hoss has done, and how it is stuff that others on this particular server have not yet done. In the great scheme of things, it is meaningless - EQ is just a game, other guilds have done before you on a Sun machine perhaps one rack away from the one you did it on. But you seem to place some importance in it, as measured by how often you talk about it. You must derive some enjoyment from it, perhaps because you have a sense of accomplishment from it. If that isn't the reason you do so, please explain why you do, because I think at this point the only way I will explain this to you is if I can put them in some framework that you can relate to.<br />
<br />
If my guess above as to why you talk about uberness so much is right, then hopefully the following makes sense to you: In the great scheme of things, VE's reputation is meaningless - EQ is just a game, other guilds have good reputations, etc. But I place importance in it, because I have a sense of accomplishment that something as large as a guild can in general do the right thing. So what we have in common is that we both take a sense of accomplishment from something in the game. You take that sense from killing mobs and doing it before others on the same server, I take that sense from killing mobs and doing it while trying to do what I perceive to be the right thing.<br />
<br />
If in the end people think I am persistent, persnickety, or even fanatic about disputing lies about my guild, that is fine by me. You don't see a lot of posts about VE on this forum precisely because we try to do the right thing.  And as I said at the start - if no other reason convinces you, take this one: The less that VE ends up in this forum, the less I have to be here, because as you have indicated, this is your house, and one in general I try to stay out of. VE's reputation in general speaks for itself, and only when someone else directly attacks it or me do I respond.</font></p>
	
	<p><p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" >__________________<br>
<b>Juergen/Enki, Guildleader, Valiant Elite</b><br />
<small><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=362626">Juergen's Stuff</a> <a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=76522">Enki's Stuff</a></small></font></p></p>
	<p></p>
