	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" >At least you finally answered my question.  <br />
<br />
<br />
If that's how you derive satisfaction from the game, then who am I to judge?<br />
<br />
However... as long as we're correcting facts here...<br />
<br />
<blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr><br />
The RA was well run and the people who administrated it made sure fair treatment was accorded to you and to the rest of the participants. The only times you got any flack was when you would demand special treatment.<br />
<hr></blockquote><br />
<br />
Demanded special treatment?  When? Where?  The only point I ever stressed is the same one I'll repeat now.<br />
<br />
If it is my best interests to cooperate with you (RA, in this case)  then I will do so.  It is not a legal/moral/ethical issue, but one of convenience.  If I get no benefit from a relationship, then I'll sever that relationship.  If I get no benefit from "playing nice" with RA, then I will no longer do so.<br />
<br />
What's in it for Hoss to "play nice" with other guilds?  Well, it's nice to be a "good neighbor" and stay out of other people's business and have them stay out of yours.  There is a tangible benefit to cooperating with others in most cases, and it's important that people maintain integrity so that others are willing to cooperate with them.<br />
<br />
That being said, I feel no need to defend my reputation to you or anyone else, and I was puzzled why it would matter so much to you.  The people who know me and deal with me on a regular basis know what kind of person I am, and their opinions are the only ones who matter to me.<br />
<br />
All the rest of ya can go fuck yourselves. :-)<br />
<br />
-Grim</font></p>
	
