	<td bgcolor="#222222" width="100%" valign="top">
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" > <b></b></font>
	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" ><blockquote><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr><br />
Ultimately, nobody remembers the loot you've won, or the mobs you've killed, or the places you've been. They'll only remember one thing...<br />
<br />
"Is this person a good guy? or a jerk?"<br />
<hr></blockquote><br />
<br />
Yeah.. It's still true.  And yes... I have changed since then.<br />
<br />
I've realized that some folks will hate ya no matter what ya do.<br />
<br />
I would like to think that the people who know me think well of me.  Ultimately, I can't make them think anything.  I can only do what I think is right.<br />
<br />
<br />
Do I think KS'ing, Plooting, Leapfrogging, and all that stuff is the sign of a bad person?  Yes I do... But...<br />
<br />
1) I don't hold it against an entire guild, just the individuals involved.<br />
<br />
2) I find it easy to forgive most things after a little time.  There's not much that happens in this game that is worth getting that upset about.<br />
<br />
I have found that a simple confrontation in the face of a seemingly rude act is usually met with a "sorry about that, my bad" and both sides move on.<br />
<br />
I've also found that the number of people on this server who engage in serious griefing is quite small, and quite well known.<br />
<br />
That's why I find the tone of most of these threads so amusing.  That's why I feel absolutely no guilt or shame about throwing down and flaming someone once in a while.  99 times out of 100 it doesn't mean anything.  The one time it does, there is usually an extraordinary circumstance.  I'm sure that if I met Juergen or Calavor or anyone else I've flamed recently, I'd most likely chuckle and offer them a beer.  It's not that important to me.<br />
<br />
That isn't to say that I don't have a point to make when I flame.  Usually it's an aggressive way of getting someone to support an argument they make. (as Juergen did in this thread)<br />
<br />
Juergen's point of view is quite understandable, even though I think it's pointless.  He spoke of putting "VE's record" against Hoss's.  Well in that vein, I'd put MY reputation up against anyone else's.  I'm not saying I'm a better player or a saint, but in the long run, I'd think that most folks would call me "one of the good guys".  I'd also be willing to bet that most folks who wouldn't, don't know me that well.<br />
<br />
Apologize not, friends won't expect it and enemies won't believe it anyway.<br />
<br />
-Grim</font></p>
	
	<p><p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" >__________________<br>
